# A valid Project-shared ruleset prints one annotated row per rule.
exec sh -c 'handrail check; echo code=$?'
stdout '^code=0$'
! stderr .
stdout '^TIER +RULE +EVENT +KIND +ACTION +STATUS$'
stdout '^project-shared +no-rm-rf-root +PreToolUse +shell +block +enabled$'
stdout '^project-shared +prefer-rg +PreToolUse +\* +warn +enabled$'

# Nested directories are scanned, local/ is not.
stdout '^project-shared +nested-rule +PostToolUse'
! stdout 'personal-only'

# Non-markdown files in the tier are ignored.
! stdout 'notes'

# Comments and blank lines in frontmatter are comments and blank lines.
stdout '^project-shared +commented +SessionStart +mcp +block +enabled$'

# Every operator negates with not_, and glob understands **.
stdout '^project-shared +negations +PostToolUse +file_edit +warn +enabled$'

-- .handrail/no-rm-rf-root.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: shell
action: block
conditions:
  - field: command
    matches: rm\s+-rf
  - any:
      - field: command
        contains: " /"
      - field: command
        starts_with: rm -rf /
---
Never delete recursively from the filesystem root. If you need to clean a
build directory, name it explicitly and stay inside the repo.
-- .handrail/prefer-rg.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
conditions:
  - field: command
    starts_with: grep
---
Use rg instead of grep.
-- .handrail/nested/nested-rule.md --
---
event: PostToolUse
conditions:
- field: path
  glob: "**/*.env"
---
Sequences at the parent's own indentation are valid YAML too.
-- .handrail/local/personal-only.md --
---
event: Stop
---
The local tier belongs to #21, not to the shared scan.
-- .handrail/commented.md --
---
# which event, and why
event: SessionStart  # trailing comments are comments

kind: mcp
action: block
conditions:
  - field: server
    equals: some-server   # so is this
  - field: command
    contains: "# not a comment"
---
A hash inside a quoted value stays part of the value.
-- .handrail/negations.md --
---
event: PostToolUse
kind: file_edit
conditions:
  - field: path
    not_glob: "**/*_test.go"
  - field: content
    not_contains: "// nolint"  # a quoted value may still carry a comment
  - field: content
    not_matches: (?i)^generated
  - field: path
    not_equals: go.sum
  - any:
      - field: path
        not_starts_with: vendor/
      - field: path
        not_ends_with: .pb.go
---
Every operator negates with not_.
-- .handrail/notes.txt --
Not a rule.
